From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: write 0x03ff, not the SROM TSSI floor, to 0x?724

In the tempsense bracket the stock driver writes 0x03ff into 0x?724 on
every core and band, also with tssifloor2g/5g removed from the NVRAM
(R7000, MMIO trace 2026-11-01). Boards without the variable got 0 here.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -4949,13 +4949,10 @@
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x0728 + s, (u16)~0x0010, 0x0010);
 	b43_phy_write(dev,   0x0736 + s, 0x0154);
 	/*
-	 * TSSI floor from the SROM. Unprogrammed (0x3ff) on every board here,
-	 * which looks like a literal; a board that programs it would be ignored
-	 * by one.
+	 * A constant, not the SROM TSSI floor: the R7000 writes 0x03ff here
+	 * with tssifloor2g/5g removed from its NVRAM too.
 	 */
-	b43_phy_write(dev,   0x0724 + s,
-		      dev->dev->bus_sprom->tssifloor5g[dev->phy.ac->pa5g_grp]
-		      & 0x03ff);
+	b43_phy_write(dev,   0x0724 + s, 0x03ff);
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x073a + s, (u16)~0x0007, g->f73a_07);
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x0725 + s, (u16)~0x0020, 0x0020);
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x0739 + s, (u16)~0x007e, g->f739_7e);
